<!--CLI Documentation — InitCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.InitCommand-->
<clidocumentation:InitCommand xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    blockml init specification
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Syntax:
        blockml init PACKAGE-FQN [--src dir] [--no-install]
    
        PACKAGE-FQN is a dotted package identifier (e.g. com.acme.bml,
        com.acme.bml.app, or com.acme), not ….Library. A `bml` segment after
        the domain is recommended so BML FQNs stay distinct from companion
        FQNs. The command parses flags, calls clicap:InitProject, and prints
        its lines. When the package FQN is missing, it also prints the short
        USAGE. InitProject does not emit USAGE. Missing or invalid FQN → exit 2
        before preflight, and writes nothing.

        Preflight is a general section. It runs before any write. --no-install
        does not skip it. A project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml
        key. An unreadable package.json fails preflight with exit 2.
        When the key is present, AGENTS.md stays and agents-md generate
        overwrites it later. When the key is absent, an existing AGENTS.md is
        renamed to AGENTS.md.pre-blockml. If that backup already exists,
        preflight exits 2 and writes nothing.

        Creates or merges package.json, writes
        Library.bml + README.bml via BomBuilder (type-as-root, no xsi/schemaLocation),
        runs npm install, then generates AGENTS.md via GenerateAgentsMd.
        Writes CLAUDE.md (@AGENTS.md) when missing. Does not load blockml.config.json.
        Does not overwrite existing BML files or CLAUDE.md. AGENTS.md is a
        generated artifact.
        Same library path already present → exit 0. Conflicting blockml.library → exit 2.
        Default runs npm install before AGENTS.md generation. --no-install skips
        both. No sections or rules leaves AGENTS.md unwritten. When --no-install
        is set and AGENTS.md is missing, the next line tells the user to run
        npm install, then npx blockml agents-md generate.
    
    Printed help:
    Usage: blockml init <package-fqn> [--src dir] [--no-install]
           blockml init --help
    
    When: turn a directory into a BlockML project. Writes a project Library, README,
    package.json blockml.library pointer, and AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md.
    
    PACKAGE-FQN is a dotted package identifier (not …Library). A bml segment after
    the domain is recommended to distinguish BML FQNs from companion FQNs.
    Preflight runs before any write and checks conditions.
    A project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml key. Then AGENTS.md
    stays, and agents-md generate overwrites it after npm install.
    Otherwise an existing AGENTS.md is renamed to AGENTS.md.pre-blockml.
    Does not overwrite existing BML files or CLAUDE.md.
    Runs npm install, then generates AGENTS.md, unless --no-install is passed.
    --no-install skips npm install and AGENTS.md generation. It does not skip preflight.
    When no AgentInstructions content is found, AGENTS.md is left unwritten.
    
    Bootstrap a new repo with npx @blockml/cli init <package-fqn>.
    Afterward use npx blockml.
    
    Related: agents-md, new, validate.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clidocumentation:NewCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:InitProject" relation="SeeAlso" />
